    bodyHtml: `<h3 class="holo-text" style="margin-bottom:12px">Ethernet &amp; Layer 2 Switching</h3>
<p style="color:var(--text-secondary);margin-bottom:16px">Ethernet is the most common LAN technology. Switches operate at Layer 2, forwarding frames based on MAC addresses.</p>

<h4 style="margin:16px 0 8px;">How a Switch Works</h4>
<div class="neu-inset" style="padding:14px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.8;">
1. <strong>Learn</strong> — Switch reads the source MAC address of incoming frames and adds it to the MAC address table with the port number<br>
2. <strong>Forward</strong> — If the destination MAC is known, forward the frame out the correct port only<br>
3. <strong>Flood</strong> — If the destination MAC is unknown (not in table), flood the frame out ALL ports except the source port<br>
4. <strong>Filter</strong> — If source and destination are on the same port, drop the frame (no need to forward)
</div>

<h4 style="margin:16px 0 8px;">MAC Address Format</h4>
<div class="neu-inset" style="padding:12px;font-size:13px;">
<code>AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF</code> — 48 bits (6 bytes), written in hexadecimal<br>
First 3 bytes = <strong>OUI</strong> (Organizationally Unique Identifier — identifies the vendor)<br>
Last 3 bytes = <strong>Device-specific</strong> (unique per device)<br>
<code>FF:FF:FF:FF:FF:FF</code> = Broadcast MAC address
</div>

<h4 style="margin:16px 0 8px;">Frame Types</h4>
<table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px;">
<tbody><tr style="background:rgba(99,102,241,0.1);"><th style="padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Type</th><th style="padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Destination</th><th style="padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Example</th></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Unicast</td><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Single specific host</td><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">PC → Server</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Broadcast</td><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">All hosts (FF:FF:FF:FF:FF:FF)</td><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">ARP request, DHCP discover</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Multicast</td><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Group of hosts</td><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">OSPF hello (01:00:5E:00:00:05)</td></tr>
</tbody></table>`,
