    title: "NAT — Network Address Translation",
    bodyHtml: `<h3 class="holo-text" style="margin-bottom:12px">NAT — Translating Private to Public IPs</h3>
<p style="color:var(--text-secondary);margin-bottom:16px">NAT allows private IP addresses (RFC 1918) to access the Internet by translating them to public IP addresses.</p>

<h4 style="margin:12px 0 8px;">NAT Types</h4>
<table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px;">
<tbody><tr style="background:rgba(99,102,241,0.1);"><th style="padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Type</th><th style="padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Description</th><th style="padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Use Case</th></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);font-weight:600;">Static NAT</td><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">1:1 mapping (one private → one public)</td><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Servers needing external access</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);font-weight:600;">Dynamic NAT</td><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Pool of public IPs assigned dynamically</td><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Multiple servers, limited public IPs</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);font-weight:600;">PAT (Overload)</td><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Many:1 using port numbers</td><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Most common — entire office shares 1 public IP</td></tr>
</tbody></table>

<div class="neu-inset" style="margin-top:16px;padding:12px;font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:1.8;">
<span style="color:var(--text-muted);">! PAT Configuration (Cisco)</span><br>
Router(config)# <span style="color:#10b981;">access-list 1 permit 192.168.1.0 0.0.0.255</span><br>
Router(config)# <span style="color:#10b981;">ip nat inside source list 1 interface gi0/0 overload</span><br>
Router(config)# <span style="color:#10b981;">interface gi0/1</span><br>
Router(config-if)# <span style="color:#3b82f6;">ip nat inside</span><br>
Router(config)# <span style="color:#10b981;">interface gi0/0</span><br>
Router(config-if)# <span style="color:#3b82f6;">ip nat outside</span>
</div>`,
