    title: "BGP — Border Gateway Protocol",
    bodyHtml: `<h3 class="holo-text" style="margin-bottom:12px">BGP — The Internet's Routing Protocol</h3>
<p style="color:var(--text-secondary);margin-bottom:16px">BGP is a path-vector protocol that routes between autonomous systems (AS). It's the protocol that makes the Internet work.</p>

<h4 style="margin:12px 0 8px;">eBGP vs iBGP</h4>
<table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px;">
<tbody><tr style="background:rgba(99,102,241,0.1);"><th style="padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Feature</th><th style="padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">eBGP</th><th style="padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">iBGP</th></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">AS</td><td style="padding:6px;">Different AS numbers</td><td style="padding:6px;">Same AS number</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">AD</td><td style="padding:6px;">20</td><td style="padding:6px;">200</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">TTL</td><td style="padding:6px;">1 (directly connected)</td><td style="padding:6px;">255</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Next-hop</td><td style="padding:6px;">Changes</td><td style="padding:6px;">Does NOT change (common issue!)</td></tr>
</tbody></table>

<h4 style="margin:16px 0 8px;">BGP Path Selection (Decision Process)</h4>
<div class="neu-inset" style="padding:14px;font-size:13px;line-height:2;">
1. Highest <strong>Weight</strong> (Cisco proprietary, local)<br>
2. Highest <strong>Local Preference</strong> (within AS)<br>
3. <strong>Locally originated</strong> (network/aggregate/redistribute)<br>
4. Shortest <strong>AS-Path</strong><br>
5. Lowest <strong>Origin</strong> (i &gt; e &gt; ?)<br>
6. Lowest <strong>MED</strong> (Multi-Exit Discriminator)<br>
7. <strong>eBGP over iBGP</strong><br>
8. Lowest <strong>IGP metric</strong> to next-hop<br>
9. Oldest <strong>eBGP route</strong><br>
10. Lowest <strong>Router ID</strong>
</div>`,
