    title: "Load Balancing Concepts",
    bodyHtml: `<h3 class="holo-text" style="margin-bottom:12px">Load Balancing — Distributing Traffic</h3>

<h4 style="margin:12px 0 8px;">Layer 4 vs Layer 7 Load Balancing</h4>
<table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px;">
<tbody><tr style="background:rgba(99,102,241,0.1);"><th style="padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Feature</th><th style="padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Layer 4 (Transport)</th><th style="padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Layer 7 (Application)</th></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Decisions based on</td><td style="padding:6px;">IP + Port only</td><td style="padding:6px;">URL, headers, cookies, content</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Speed</td><td style="padding:6px;">Very fast (no inspection)</td><td style="padding:6px;">Slower (deep inspection)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">SSL Termination</td><td style="padding:6px;">Pass-through</td><td style="padding:6px;">Yes (offload SSL from servers)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Use Cases</td><td style="padding:6px;">TCP/UDP apps, databases</td><td style="padding:6px;">Web apps, APIs, microservices</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Examples</td><td style="padding:6px;">AWS NLB, Azure LB</td><td style="padding:6px;">AWS ALB, Nginx, HAProxy, F5</td></tr>
</tbody></table>

<h4 style="margin:16px 0 8px;">Load Balancing Algorithms</h4>
<div class="neu-inset" style="padding:14px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.8;">
<strong style="color:#3b82f6;">Round Robin:</strong> Equal distribution, one after another (A→B→C→A→B→C)<br>
<strong style="color:#10b981;">Weighted Round Robin:</strong> More traffic to powerful servers (A:3, B:1, C:1)<br>
<strong style="color:#f59e0b;">Least Connections:</strong> Send to server with fewest active connections<br>
<strong style="color:#8b5cf6;">IP Hash:</strong> Same client always goes to same server (session persistence)<br>
<strong style="color:#ef4444;">Least Response Time:</strong> Send to fastest responding server<br>
<strong style="color:#ec4899;">Random:</strong> Random selection (surprisingly effective at scale)
</div>

<h4 style="margin:16px 0 8px;">Health Checks</h4>
<div class="neu-inset" style="padding:12px;font-size:13px;">
LB periodically checks if backend servers are alive:<br>
• <strong>TCP check:</strong> Can I connect to port 80? (basic)<br>
• <strong>HTTP check:</strong> Does /health return 200 OK? (application-aware)<br>
• <strong>Content check:</strong> Does the response contain "OK"? (deep)<br>
Failed checks → server removed from pool → traffic rerouted
</div>`,
