    bodyHtml: `<h3 class="holo-text" style="margin-bottom:12px">802.1X — Port-Based Network Access Control</h3>
<p style="color:var(--text-secondary);margin-bottom:16px">802.1X ensures only authenticated devices can access the network. It's a key component of Zero Trust architecture.</p>

<h4 style="margin:12px 0 8px;">802.1X Components</h4>
<table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px;">
<tbody><tr style="background:rgba(99,102,241,0.1);"><th style="padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Component</th><th style="padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Role</th><th style="padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Example</th></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);font-weight:600;">Supplicant</td><td style="padding:6px;">Client requesting access</td><td style="padding:6px;">Windows PC, Laptop, Phone</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);font-weight:600;">Authenticator</td><td style="padding:6px;">Network device enforcing access</td><td style="padding:6px;">Switch, Wireless AP</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);font-weight:600;">Authentication Server</td><td style="padding:6px;">Validates credentials via RADIUS</td><td style="padding:6px;">Cisco ISE, Microsoft NPS, FreeRADIUS</td></tr>
</tbody></table>

<h4 style="margin:16px 0 8px;">EAP Methods</h4>
<table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px;">
<tbody><tr style="background:rgba(99,102,241,0.1);"><th style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Method</th><th style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Auth Type</th><th style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Security</th><th style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Common Use</th></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">EAP-TLS</td><td style="padding:6px;">Mutual certificate</td><td style="padding:6px;color:#10b981;">Highest</td><td style="padding:6px;">Enterprise (both sides have certs)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">PEAP (MSCHAPv2)</td><td style="padding:6px;">Username/password in TLS tunnel</td><td style="padding:6px;color:#3b82f6;">High</td><td style="padding:6px;">Most common — Windows AD</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">EAP-FAST</td><td style="padding:6px;">Cisco — PAC-based</td><td style="padding:6px;color:#3b82f6;">High</td><td style="padding:6px;">Cisco environments</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">MAB</td><td style="padding:6px;">MAC Authentication Bypass</td><td style="padding:6px;color:#f59e0b;">Low</td><td style="padding:6px;">Printers, IoT (no 802.1X support)</td></tr>
</tbody></table>

<div class="neu-inset" style="margin-top:16px;padding:14px;">
<strong>💡 Deployment Order:</strong><br>
1. Deploy RADIUS server (ISE/NPS)<br>
2. Start in "monitor mode" (log but don't block)<br>
3. Create policies (authorize known devices)<br>
4. Move to "low-impact mode" (block unknown, allow critical services)<br>
5. Finally "closed mode" (full enforcement)
</div>`,
