    bodyHtml: `<h3 class="holo-text" style="margin-bottom:12px">Enterprise Network Design</h3>

<h4 style="margin:12px 0 8px;">Cisco 3-Tier Architecture</h4>
<div class="neu-inset" style="padding:14px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.8;">
<strong style="color:#ef4444;">Core Layer:</strong> High-speed backbone — fast forwarding, NO filtering, NO ACLs here<br>
<strong style="color:#f59e0b;">Distribution Layer:</strong> Policy enforcement — routing, filtering, ACLs, QoS, redundancy<br>
<strong style="color:#10b981;">Access Layer:</strong> User-facing — port security, VLANs, PoE, DHCP snooping, 802.1X
</div>

<h4 style="margin:16px 0 8px;">Collapsed Core (2-Tier)</h4>
<div class="neu-inset" style="padding:14px;font-size:13px;">
For smaller networks: combine Core + Distribution into one layer.<br>
<strong>Access → Distribution/Core</strong><br>
Common in branch offices and SMBs with fewer than 200 users.
</div>

<h4 style="margin:16px 0 8px;">Spine-Leaf (Data Center)</h4>
<div class="neu-inset" style="padding:14px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.8;">
Modern data center design replacing 3-tier:<br>
<strong>Spine:</strong> L3 switches — every spine connects to every leaf<br>
<strong>Leaf:</strong> ToR switches — servers connect here<br>
<strong>Benefits:</strong> Equal-cost paths, predictable latency, easy to scale horizontally<br>
<strong>Used with:</strong> VXLAN + EVPN for overlay networking
</div>

<h4 style="margin:16px 0 8px;">Design Best Practices</h4>
<div class="neu-inset" style="padding:14px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.8;">
✅ <strong>Redundancy:</strong> No single point of failure (dual uplinks, HSRP/VRRP, EtherChannel)<br>
✅ <strong>Segmentation:</strong> VLANs + firewall zones to limit blast radius<br>
✅ <strong>Scalability:</strong> Design for 2x current capacity<br>
✅ <strong>Documentation:</strong> Diagrams, IP plans, change logs<br>
✅ <strong>Standardization:</strong> Same config templates across all similar devices<br>
✅ <strong>Security in depth:</strong> Multiple layers of security (edge FW + internal FW + NAC + IPS)<br>
✅ <strong>Monitoring:</strong> SNMP, syslog, NetFlow, SIEM from day 1
</div>`,
