    title: "Systematic Troubleshooting Mastery",
    bodyHtml: `<h3 class="holo-text" style="margin-bottom:12px">The Art of Network Troubleshooting</h3>

<h4 style="margin:12px 0 8px;">The 8-Step Troubleshooting Method</h4>
<div class="neu-inset" style="padding:14px;font-size:13px;line-height:2;">
<strong style="color:#ef4444;">1. Define the Problem</strong> — Get specifics: who, what, when, where, how often?<br>
<strong style="color:#f59e0b;">2. Gather Information</strong> — Logs, show commands, user reports, monitoring tools<br>
<strong style="color:#eab308;">3. Analyze Data</strong> — What changed? When did it start? What's the scope?<br>
<strong style="color:#10b981;">4. Eliminate Possibilities</strong> — Use OSI layer approach (test each layer)<br>
<strong style="color:#3b82f6;">5. Propose a Hypothesis</strong> — "I think the issue is X because Y"<br>
<strong style="color:#8b5cf6;">6. Test the Hypothesis</strong> — Make ONE change and test<br>
<strong style="color:#ec4899;">7. Solve the Problem</strong> — Implement the fix, verify it works<br>
<strong style="color:#6366f1;">8. Document</strong> — Record the problem, cause, solution, and prevention
</div>

<h4 style="margin:16px 0 8px;">Common Mistakes</h4>
<div class="neu-inset" style="padding:14px;font-size:13px;line-height:1.8;">
❌ <strong>Changing multiple things at once</strong> — Can't identify what fixed it<br>
❌ <strong>Assuming without testing</strong> — "It must be the firewall" → Test it!<br>
❌ <strong>Ignoring recent changes</strong> — 90% of issues follow a change<br>
❌ <strong>Not checking the simple stuff</strong> — Is the cable plugged in? Is the interface up?<br>
❌ <strong>Not documenting</strong> — Same issue will happen again and you won't remember
</div>

<h4 style="margin:16px 0 8px;">Essential Troubleshooting Tools</h4>
<table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px;">
<tbody><tr style="background:rgba(99,102,241,0.1);"><th style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Tool</th><th style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">Purpose</th><th style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);">When to Use</th></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);font-weight:600;">ping</td><td style="padding:6px;">Test reachability (ICMP)</td><td style="padding:6px;">First test — is it reachable?</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);font-weight:600;">traceroute</td><td style="padding:6px;">Show hop-by-hop path</td><td style="padding:6px;">Where does the packet stop?</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);font-weight:600;">nslookup/dig</td><td style="padding:6px;">DNS resolution test</td><td style="padding:6px;">Name resolution issues</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);font-weight:600;">Wireshark</td><td style="padding:6px;">Packet capture &amp; analysis</td><td style="padding:6px;">Deep protocol debugging</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);font-weight:600;">netstat/ss</td><td style="padding:6px;">Show connections &amp; ports</td><td style="padding:6px;">Is the service listening?</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);font-weight:600;">telnet/nc</td><td style="padding:6px;">Test TCP port connectivity</td><td style="padding:6px;">Is port X open on host Y?</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);font-weight:600;">SNMP/NMS</td><td style="padding:6px;">Device monitoring</td><td style="padding:6px;">Performance trends, alerts</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);font-weight:600;">syslog</td><td style="padding:6px;">Centralized log collection</td><td style="padding:6px;">Correlate events across devices</td></tr>
</tbody></table>`,
