    bodyHtml: `<h3 class="holo-text" style="margin-bottom:12px">SD-WAN — The Future of Enterprise WAN</h3>
<p style="color:var(--text-secondary);margin-bottom:16px">SD-WAN decouples the control plane from data plane, enabling centralized management, dynamic path selection, and direct internet breakout. It's replacing traditional MPLS WAN.</p>

<h4 style="color:#9333ea;margin:16px 0 8px;">SD-WAN vs Traditional WAN</h4>
<table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px;">
<tbody><tr style="background:rgba(147,51,234,0.1);"><th style="padding:8px;text-align:left;">Feature</th><th style="padding:8px;text-align:left;">Traditional WAN</th><th style="padding:8px;text-align:left;">SD-WAN</th></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);font-weight:600;">Transport</td><td style="padding:6px;">MPLS only</td><td style="padding:6px;">MPLS + Internet + LTE/5G</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);font-weight:600;">Management</td><td style="padding:6px;">CLI per device</td><td style="padding:6px;">Central controller (GUI)</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);font-weight:600;">Path Selection</td><td style="padding:6px;">Static routing</td><td style="padding:6px;">Dynamic per-app SLA</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--glass-border);font-weight:600;">Cloud Access</td><td style="padding:6px;">Backhaul to DC</td><td style="padding:6px;">Direct Internet Breakout</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;font-weight:600;">Cost</td><td style="padding:6px;">$$$$ (MPLS circuits)</td><td style="padding:6px;">$$ (broadband + LTE)</td></tr>
</tbody></table>

<h4 style="color:#9333ea;margin:16px 0 8px;">SD-WAN Architecture</h4>
<div style="background:#0a0a0a;border-radius:8px;padding:12px;font-family:monospace;font-size:11px;color:#00ff41;">
<pre style="margin:0;">         vManage (Orchestrator)
   Policy | Config | Monitor | Templates
                   |
         vSmart Controller(s)
   Route Policy | OMP | Data Policy
        |                    |
   vEdge/cEdge          vEdge/cEdge
   Branch-1  &lt;--IPsec--&gt;  Branch-2
   MPLS|Internet|LTE     MPLS|Internet|LTE</pre>
</div>

<h4 style="color:#9333ea;margin:16px 0 8px;">Application-Aware Routing</h4>
<div style="background:var(--glass-bg);border-radius:8px;padding:12px;font-size:12px;">
<table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;">
<tbody><tr style="background:rgba(147,51,234,0.05);"><th style="padding:6px;text-align:left;">Application</th><th style="padding:6px;text-align:left;">SLA Policy</th><th style="padding:6px;text-align:left;">Primary Path</th><th style="padding:6px;text-align:left;">Fallback</th></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;">Voice/Video</td><td style="padding:6px;">Latency &lt;150ms, Loss &lt;1%</td><td style="padding:6px;">MPLS</td><td style="padding:6px;">LTE</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;">O365/SaaS</td><td style="padding:6px;">Latency &lt;200ms</td><td style="padding:6px;">Direct Internet</td><td style="padding:6px;">MPLS</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:6px;">Backup/Bulk</td><td style="padding:6px;">Best effort</td><td style="padding:6px;">Internet</td><td style="padding:6px;">Any</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>

<div style="margin-top:12px;padding:10px;border-left:3px solid #9333ea;background:rgba(147,51,234,0.05);border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;">
<strong style="color:#9333ea;">Master Tip:</strong> <span style="font-size:13px;">SD-WAN's killer feature is per-packet path selection based on real-time SLA. If MPLS degrades, voice automatically shifts to LTE within seconds — no human intervention.</span>
</div>`,
